  "comments": [
    {"at":0,"placement":"line","text":"Exchanges the point shape_x0/shape_y0 with shape_x1/shape_y1, so that the circle code uses the second point as the centre. The radius is the distance of the points in X plus the distance in Y, at most max_y. point_x0 and circle_dy get the radius, circle_dx gets 0."},
    {"at":68,"placement":"line","text":"Draws the circle of shape_x0/y0 and shape_x1/y1 with the XOR plot ($18c2): the rubber circle of the Circle and Disc tools. Keeps the shape points and the circle points ($3e-$41)."},
    {"at":68,"placement":"side","text":"circle_step_vector = $3d49: plots 4 points at each step."},
    {"at":139,"placement":"line","text":"Draws the circle of shape_x0/y0 and shape_x1/y1 with the brush ($17ad)."},
    {"at":170,"placement":"line","text":"Draws the disc of shape_x0/y0 and shape_x1/y1 with the brush: circle_step_vector = $3cde, which draws 2 lines at each step."},
    {"at":181,"placement":"line","text":"Steps through a quarter of the circle with the midpoint method: circle_dy starts at the radius, circle_dx at 0, the error (point_x1/point_y1) at 2 - 2 * radius. It calls the routine of circle_step_vector for each point. That routine ends the loop when circle_dy is 0."},
    {"at":216,"placement":"line","text":"Circle loop: chooses the next step from the sign of circle_error."},
    {"at":220,"placement":"side","text":"Error 0: diagonal step."},
    {"at":224,"placement":"side","text":"Error < 0."},
    {"at":229,"placement":"line","text":"Error < 0: t = 2 * error + 2 * circle_y_offset - 1 (in cursor_x/cursor_y). t <= 0: horizontal step, else diagonal step."},
    {"at":243,"placement":"side","text":"cursor_x/cursor_y hold the 16-bit value t."},
    {"at":273,"placement":"line","text":"Horizontal step: circle_x_offset + 1, plot, error + 2 * circle_x_offset + 1."},
    {"at":291,"placement":"line","text":"Diagonal step: circle_x_offset + 1, circle_y_offset - 1, plot, error + 2 * circle_x_offset - 2 * circle_y_offset + 2."},
    {"at":323,"placement":"line","text":"Vertical step: circle_y_offset - 1, plot, error - 2 * circle_y_offset + 1."},
    {"at":343,"placement":"line","text":"Error > 0: t = 2 * error - 2 * circle_x_offset - 1. t <= 0: diagonal step, else vertical step."},
    {"at":387,"placement":"line","text":"Writes 2 * circle_error to cursor_x/cursor_y (a 16-bit work value)."},
    {"at":399,"placement":"line","text":"Decrements the 16-bit value in cursor_x/cursor_y. Output: A = the high byte (cursor_y), with the N and Z flags of it."},
    {"at":410,"placement":"line","text":"Jumps through circle_plot_vector. The plot routine ends the circle (it drops the return address of circle_plot) when circle_y_offset is 0."}
  ],
